  rung 0  (F diag, Theta diag, Sigma diag)   logL = 656.3578127682

=== Entry gate: the factorisation contract ===

At r = 0 with diagonal Phi, Theta and Sigma the likelihood factorises,
so the joint fit must equal the sum of the univariate fits exactly.

  univariate 1 (p=2, q=0)   logL =     147.9767602488
  univariate 2 (p=2, q=0)   logL =     253.5424657685
  univariate 3 (p=2, q=0)   logL =     254.8385867509
                                 sum  =     656.3578127682
                                 joint=     656.3578127682
  (both sides untruncated; the fit's own logL, xi truncated at 1e-03, is 656.3578127682)

  crossing identity (joint - sum) = -2.444e-11   (tolerance 1.0e-06)   VERIFIED
  rung 1  (F diag, Theta diag, Sigma free)   logL = 669.9608176531
  rung 2  (F free, Theta free, Sigma free)   logL = 721.1988081448

